            <div xml:id="d340">

                <pb facs="0495" n="381" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg381"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/5611: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cunningham</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-10-13T10:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 13,
                                1924—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 13—2:43
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>… source of most reliable police information during war states that Generals Lu
                    and Ho have deserted possibly going about 3 a.m. today. Will report later
                    whether confirmation obtained.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
